{"type":"text","timestamp":1793647726287,"sessionID":"ses_e6244514affec1KZABmknDJCOV","part":{"id":"prt_19dbc3d4e001QT26s8VWRAk8yI_text-0","sessionID":"ses_e6244514affec1KZABmknDJCOV","messageID":"msg_19dbc3d4e001QT26s8VWRAk8yI","type":"text","text":"\n\n**Recommendation: ship B.**\n\n**[goal]** Decide A vs B for the Pixel Arena tutorial from ./telemetry and record result.json.\n\n**[action]** Cleaned per README (dedupe by `session_id`: 1870 rows → 1800 unique sessions, 70 ETL resends removed, zero conflicts; variants normalized for case/leading space; 900 per arm). Primary test: pooled two-proportion z-test on completion. Robustness: Fisher exact, and player-level checks because 366 of 763 players appear in both variants (session-level randomization, so the session test overstates independence).\n\n**[result]**\n- A: 342/900 = 38.0%; B: 420/900 = 46.7%; +8.7pp; z=3.72, p=0.000198 (Fisher p=0.00024).\n- Paired McNemar on first-session pairs of crossover players: 112 B-only vs 77 A-only completions, exact p=0.013.\n- Within-player mean diff on crossover players: +9.0pp, t=2.80 (n=366); order balanced (184 A-first vs 182 B-first), so carryover is not a systematic bias.\n- Single-variant-players-only subset: +6.4pp, same direction, underpowered (n=397, p=0.20).\n- Every independence-safe analysis points the same way; the release rule (significant at 5%) is met. Written to `result.json`: `ship_b=true, sessions_a=900, sessions_b=900, completion_rate_a=0.38, completion_rate_b=0.4667, p_value=0.000198`.\n\nAssumptions: `p_value` in result.json is the primary pre-registered-style session-level test per the README rule; completion is the decision metric; two-sided tests.\n\n**[next]** Flag the design flaw for the next test: randomize per player, not per session.\n\nHow I know it's right: scripts (`analyze.py`, `check2.py`, `check3.py`) run on the raw CSV with quoted outputs above; the dedup count, conflicting-dupe check, and all four statistical views were read from actual output, and `result.json` was re-read after writing.","time":{"start":1793647721825,"end":1793647726287}}}

